I updated the canonical plan to reflect the current experiment blockers and the G-PREP implementation state. The CPU contract is implemented and passes focused tests; native-model quality and a complete real-checkpoint decode remain unverified.

- **Mask pilot:** the C-01 card records that YOLO26x is only one completed arm. SAM3.1 and a useful hybrid still need the same-window PointStream encode/decode, quality, byte, speed, memory, and image evidence; their blocker is documented. Cached masks remain imperfect references. :codex-annotation{index="1"}
- **Learned baseline:** R-03 records that an isolated DCVC-UF setup is authorized, but checkpoint downloads currently return 403 and the recorded host cannot run its documented CUDA stack. No result is claimed. :codex-annotation{index="2"}
- **Fixed-resolution generators:** G-PREP now applies to MTTF and every other fixed-input generator. The shared code blackens the charged reference crop, aligns spatial conditions, and removes padding from declared canvas outputs. MTTF still has no adapter, and real-checkpoint behavior remains to be tested. :codex-annotation{index="3"}

The implementation is in [stages.py](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/src/runner/stages.py), [dispatch.py](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/src/pipeline/reconstruction/dispatch.py), and the generation adapters. I updated [PLAN.md](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/PLAN.md), the [generation area](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/docs/areas/generation.md), and the [journal experiment plan](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/docs/strategy/journal-experiment-plan.md).

Targeted pytest checks, Ruff, and `git diff --check` passed. The optional `compileall` check could not write to the harness’s read-only bytecode cache; the tests imported the changed modules. I also rechecked the GPU gate: `nvidia-smi` still cannot communicate with the driver, so no GPU pilot ran.

The documentation now reflects the verified state, and a two-anchor R-02 check is preregistered. **No new AV1/VVC anchors were encoded, so Antigravity’s claimed Pareto win remains unverified.**

A read-only check confirmed that FFmpeg decodes VVC: it decoded all 48 frames of an existing 3840×2160 stream. The registered C-01 input PNG hashes also still match, though the MP4 now at the recorded source path has a different hash; the planned comparison must use the cached PNGs directly. The R-02 plan and manifest record those details and the required output-preserving procedure: [experiment plan](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/docs/strategy/journal-experiment-plan.md:123), [evaluation record](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/docs/areas/evaluation.md:242), [preregistration](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/manifests/journal_20260925_r02_sinner_alcaraz002_16f.json:1).

The GPU query still fails. The host rule in `/home/itec/emanuele/.agent-rules/AGENTS.md` requires verifying a free GPU before **any** experiment, including CPU-only work, so R-02 remains preregistered but unlaunched. `git diff --check` and manifest validation passed.

The existing YOLO26x arm has a real PointStream encode/decode and inspection sheets, but no paired SAM3.1/hybrid run or matched AV1/VVC comparison. Its cached masks are imperfect evaluation references, and it establishes no codec win. :codex-annotation{index="1"}

![C-01 YOLO26x source, mask overlays, and decoded output](/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream-data/outputs/journal-20260925/c01-gpu/sinner-alcaraz-scene002-first16-yolo26x-fast-run1/contact-frame-008.png)

DCVC-UF remains uninstalled: the official checkpoint links returned HTTP 403, and the documented CUDA stack is incompatible with the recorded host. The docs correctly leave setup paused until both weights and a compatible host are available. :codex-annotation{index="2"}

G-PREP is already recorded as the common protocol for fixed-resolution generators, including MTTF: segment onto black, resize with aspect ratio preserved, pad to the model dimensions, then invert placement and account for transmitted masks and geometry. :codex-annotation{index="3"}
